  "body": "## Scope and task card\n\nResearch base: main `a18b4b0136d647529971e9fcb99fa83f5b9a0b81`; the branch is rebased onto main `0b1cccf8` with all pinned inputs unchanged. The selected #1094 record is unchanged. Chooser nonce `1f0be36e3f2ed2c4ea3d763eb52aedc1` drew the revision-3 `formal-interface-lemma` card. It is **refined** to a theorem-to-certificate audit of PR1212 (Brett Halligan / @burntout76 and Ninefold, head `57099cb5`, now on main as `research/complex-rank8-decoder-rigidity/`): \u00a710's stabilizer transport and \u00a78's bridge from gauge rigidity to PR968's eight-term floor. PR1670 (session 16 of this run) audited PR1560 and explicitly left these two sections uncovered.\n\n## Precise delta\n\nAdds only `research/e8-rank8-transport-audit/`. No predecessor, selected or `upstream/` changes.\n\n- **\u00a710 transport, recomputed independently.** The 120 E8 lines are built from scratch, without PR1212's group code. The verifier checks 2,025 frames (one Weyl orbit), 204 one/two-reflection maps fixing `FRAME0`, signed Gram transport for every generator (binary pairing preserved), one orbit on the 112 P112 lines, and orbits 28/336/896 on the 1,260 second frames, typed (4,4)/(2,2,2,2)/(1\u2078). It also places PR717's P104 in the 896 orbit and rechecks PR1212's published (2,2,2,2) unit and pivot.\n- **Alternate pivot for type (4,4).** The unit is PR1212's own representative: delete `FRAME0` and `{2,3,16,17,46,47,52,53}` (PR1212 numbering). Of its 801 live pivots, 25 leave no class incomplete. PR1212's pivot `{4,5,14,15,48,49,50,51}` covers 12 of 14 blocks, and **24 others cover all 14**. That contradicts PR1212 \u00a710's remark that other pivots \"leave eight classes incomplete\". At `{12,13,22,23,30,31,36,37}`, which is also PR1212's (2,2,2,2) pivot, the checks give:\n  - 288 Lemma 5 group witnesses;\n  - 56 Steiner triples and 24 Hadamard classes;\n  - 1,952 ordered Lemma 6 sign-rule checks;\n  - an independently encoded two-term + diagonal zero-pattern CNF (1,152 variables, 16,865 clauses with `some zero`), refuted by a 2,501-addition DRUP proof from Lingeling that a stdlib RUP checker replays.\n\n  PR1212's original Lemmas 5\u20137 then give rank-eight gauge rigidity for this unit, and the transport extends it to all 28.\n- **What is new.** This is a **second proof of a theorem PR1389 already established**. PR1389 kept PR1212's 12-block pivot, added gluing Lemma 6\u2032, and relied on PR1212's four-family zero exclusion. The alternate route needs only the original Lemmas 5\u20137 and the two-family certificate.\n- **\u00a78 written audit.** Eight costly terms of a gauge-rigid rank-eight E-graph matrix have the same supports as an exact all-pairs decoder `(RA,RB)`, so PR968's real floor applies. At p=16 that floor is PR968(a)'s `\u226556`; (b)'s `72\u2212p` is stated only for p\u226415. A complex COPY floor needs the separate complex extension.\n\n## Review by Claude (session 19): what changed\n\nCodex ran out of usage mid-edit. Its notes, README, PROOF and `RESULT.json` described an earlier run that had deleted the **wrong frame**: the 28-orbit's minimum, which is PR1212's *pivot* frame, labelled as PR1212's deleted frame. Codex fixed the binding in `verify.py` and regenerated the CNF and proof, but did not update anything else. The shipped verifier then failed its receipt comparison. In review I:\n- regenerated `RESULT.json`;\n- corrected PROOF/README/TASK (deleted frame, digests, 2,501 lemmas instead of 2,910, proof size);\n- made the verifier require the displayed pivot to equal PR1212's `{12,\u2026,37}` and record both numberings;\n- strengthened the gluing check from a count to PR1212's exact sign rule, in both orders;\n- made the PASS marker report computed counts;\n- pinned PR1212's PROOF.md at its main path (byte-identical blob `5940f280`) instead of a vendored copy.\n\n**Independent cross-check, not part of the package.** PR1212's own code (`extension_units`, `blocks_relative`, `build_zero_cnf`) run on the same unit confirms:\n- the (24,0,12) and 24\u00d7(24,0,14) pivot census;\n- D1/D2 witnesses at the new pivot;\n- with CaDiCaL, the reduced two+diag CNF is UNSAT with `some zero` and SAT without it at the new pivot, and SAT at PR1212's pivot, matching its Lemma 8.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -I -B research/e8-rank8-transport-audit/verify.py\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/e8-rank8-transport-audit\n```\n\nStdlib only, about 5 s; passes on 3.10, 3.12 and optimized 3.14. Controls reject a Gram-sign change, a corrupted transport permutation, the proof without `some zero`, an injected non-RUP unit and a truncated proof.\n\n## Limits, overlap and credit\n\nNot covered: a new COPY floor, \u03ba change, complex COPY floor, nine or more costly terms, or a proof-assistant formalization. PR1212's written Lemmas 5\u20137 and PR968's cited flat classification (F6) are relied on, not reproved. PR1497 separately audits Lemmas 5\u20136. A live overlap refresh (451 open PRs, 417 discussions, 2026-10-14 05:55 EDT) found PR1389 (priority for the theorem), PR1670 (complementary) and @1337isnot1337's all-pivot census of an admissible P104 unit in discussion 1163, which is a methodological precedent on a different orbit.\n\n**Open next questions:** (1) Can this pivot shorten a formalization of type-(4,4) rigidity? (2) Does the two-family refutation at this pivot have a short readable core? At PR1212's pivot the same two families do not exclude zeros.\n\nCredit: Brett Halligan / @burntout76 and Ninefold (PR1212); PR1389 (Josie Elliston, Claude-assisted); PR1497's auditors; @themilkman216 (PR968); DreamingOfClouds (PR717); @an664 (PR1560) for the surrounding rigidity line.\n\nPrepared for Josie Elliston (@JosieElliston) by **OpenAI Codex** (offline session 17b of an overnight donated run: audit, verifier, proof generation, controls, writing). **Claude** (Anthropic, session 19) reviewed, corrected and published it. Substantial AI assistance; no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
